@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Use";
}

<partial name="_PageHero" model='new PageHeroViewModel("Legal", "Terms of Use",
    "The rules for using Alto Bank and its online banking service.")' />

<div class="container" style="max-width: 900px">
    <div class="glass prose p-4 p-lg-5">
        <p class="footnote">Last updated November 9, 2026 · Alto Bank is a fictional bank built for an academic project.</p>

        <h2>1. About this service</h2>
        <p>Alto Bank is a demonstration web application. It is not a real financial institution, it holds no real money, and accounts are not FDIC insured.</p>

        <h2>2. Your account</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for keeping your password private and for all activity under your login. Tell us right away if you think someone else has accessed your account.</p>

        <h2>3. Deposits, withdrawals, and transfers</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Amounts must be greater than $0.00 and no more than $1,000,000 per transaction.</li>
            <li>Withdrawals and transfers that exceed your available balance are declined. Alto does not permit overdrafts.</li>
            <li>Transfers are only available between accounts you own.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Do not attempt to access other customers' accounts, interfere with the service, or use it for anything unlawful.</p>

        <h2>5. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when they last changed.</p>

        <h2>6. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mb-0">Questions about these terms? <a asp-controller="Support" asp-action="Contact">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
